@startuml
title SD3 : Consent applied by message class

actor Recipient
participant "Marketing" as MKT
participant "Billing Account Management" as BAM
participant "//Communication Interaction Management//" as CIM
participant "Channel Transport" as CT

== marketing — message class permits suppression ==
MKT -> CIM : 1 **TMF681** POST /communicationMessage\n(receiver[].party.id="Alice",\ncontent="Upgrade to 1 Gbps for EUR 5 a month",\ncharacteristic[messageClass="marketing"])
activate CIM
CIM -> CIM : 2 Alice withdrew marketing consent at SD-2;\nmessage class permits suppression
CIM --> MKT : 3 **TMF681** 201 Created\n(state="cancelled")
deactivate CIM
note right of CIM
  Recorded and cancelled rather than discarded, so that
  suppression appears in the delivery record (Q2, Q4).
end note

== arrears — message class does not permit suppression ==
BAM -> CIM : 4 **TMF681** POST /communicationMessage\n(receiver[].party.id="Alice",\ncontent="Your account is EUR 48.60 overdue ...",\ncharacteristic[messageClass="regulatory"], priority="high")
activate CIM
CIM -> CIM : 5 same recipient, same consent state;\nmessage class does not permit suppression
CIM -> CT : 6 dispatch on the SMS transport
activate CT
CT --> Recipient : 7 "Your account is EUR 48.60 overdue. Pay by\n26 Sep to avoid restriction."
CT --> CIM : 8 **transport receipt** delivered,\ntimestamp
deactivate CT
CIM --> BAM : 9 **TMF681** 200 OK (state="completed")
deactivate CIM

note across
  One recipient, one consent state, two outcomes,
  determined by message class at the point of dispatch (C2).
  Neither Marketing nor Account Management holds the consent
  state or the class policy, and neither was changed.
end note

@enduml
